 "equipment_type": "Dedicated outdoor air unit (DOAS) controller",
 "applies_to": "Carrier 62H 03-55 ton dedicated outdoor air units with Revision K controls (100% outdoor air).",
 "summary": "62H dedicated outdoor air units with Revision K controls use an Automated Logic LS-1628u controller that speaks BACnet MS/TP on its RS-485 ports and BACnet IP on its Gig-E port. The Table C mapping lists 251 AVs, BVs and two MSVs: occupancy and BAS heartbeat points, supply air, zone and dehumidification setpoints, sensor readings, digital compressor output, compressor, fan, wheel and damper status, PID override points and many individual alarms.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Revision K controls",
 "default_device_instance": 1602,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The mapping table has no units column, so units are left blank; defaults quoted in the table's descriptions are added to the descriptions here.",
  "Appendix B Table D (operating modes): 0 SCHEDULE, 1 OA DAMPER, 2 FAN ONLY, 3 ECONOMIZER, 4 COOLING, 5 CLG and REHEAT, 6 DEHUMID, 7 HEATING, 8 HEAT PUMP, 9 AUX HEAT, 10 EMER HEAT, 11 DEFROST ON, 12 PURGE #1, 13 PURGE#2, 14 FDD ALARM, 15 SF FAIL, 16 SF HAND, 17 EF FAIL, 18 EF HAND, 19 C1 ALARM, 20 C1 STOP, 21 HPS1 ALARM, 22 APS2 STOP, 23 LPS1 ALARM, 24 LPS1 STOP, 25 FP1 ALARM, 26 FP1 STOP, 27 C1 HAND, 28 C2 ALARM, 29 C2 STOP, 30 HPS2 ALARM, 31 HPS2 STOP, 32 LPS2 ALARM, 33 LPS2 STOP, 34 FP2 ALARM, 35 FP2 STOP, 36 C2 HAND, 37 HEAT FAIL, 38 HIGH SAT, 39 WFS ALARM, 40 FZT ALARM, 41 RUN TIME, 42 SP OVERLAP, 43 SENSOR FAIL, 44 CLGD FLTR, 45 COS ALARM, 46 HIGH CO2, 47 HIGH SFDPT, 48 SD STOP, 49 SAT FAIL, 50 LOW SAT, 51 DISABLED, 52 ENERGY MGT, 53 EMERSHTDN.",
  "Appendix B Table E (operating conditions): 0 UNOCCUPIED, 1 NIGHT STBK, 2 OPT START, 3 OCCUPIED, 4 TESTING, 5 ALARM, 6 SHUTDOWN.",
  "The table sends Operating Condition (AV 111) to Table D and Operating Mode (AV 112) to Table E, but Table D is titled Operating Modes and Table E Operating Conditions; the names suggest AV 112 uses Table D and AV 111 Table E. Check on the unit.",
  "Many objects only apply with the matching option (energy wheel, exhaust fan, hot gas reheat, heat pump, chilled water valve, airflow stations, CO2).",
  "Same table as the 62X/62W Rev. K manuals plus three digital compressor points: DIG1 Minimum Output (AV 647), Digital Compressor #1 Percent (AV 6401) and #2 Percent (AV 6501)."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "62H 03-55 Tons Revision K Controls Dedicated Outdoor Air Unit - Controls, Operation, Start-Up, and Troubleshooting (Appendix A, Table C: Mapping Points - Carrier 62H Rev. K - 100% Outdoor Air)",
  "doc_number": "62H-2T",
  "revision_date": "4-26",
  "url": "https://brandportal.carrier.com/asset/07ef7df6-5ec8-4570-a4dd-84659551da6c/62H-2T.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The 62H uses an Automated Logic LS-1628u controller (third-party to i-Vu). Set Occupancy Control Options to BAS, then command occupancy with BAS Manual Occ Control and toggle Field BAS Comm. Status faster than the BAS lost delay. Write the supply air setpoints the unit discharges to, read operating mode, occupancy, SAT and the alarm status.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 101",
    "name": "occ_en",
    "why": "BAS occupied/unoccupied command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 101",
    "name": "occ_ctrl_opts",
    "why": "Must be BAS for BAS occupancy control"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 313",
    "name": "clg_sat_sp_o",
    "why": "Occupied cooling supply air setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 354",
    "name": "htg_sat_sp_o",
    "why": "Occupied heating supply air setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 110",
    "name": "bas_comm_status",
    "why": "Heartbeat: toggle before the BAS lost delay ends"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 900",
    "name": "alarm_reset",
    "why": "Alarm reset"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 112",
    "name": "op_mode",
    "why": "Operating mode code (Appendix B)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 105",
    "name": "occ_status",
    "why": "Occupied/unoccupied status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 235",
    "name": "sat_stat",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 851",
    "name": "alarm_status",
    "why": "Unit alarm status"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Occupancy Control (Occupancy Control Options, MSV 101) chooses BAS control, local schedule, 24/7 or CO2. With BAS control, BAS Manual Occ Control (BV 101) puts the unit in occupied or unoccupied mode. Enable Unit Operation (Tech Set Up) must be on. Emergency Shutdown in Tech Set Up disables the unit; Emerg. Shutdown Enable (BV 821) is writable over BACnet.",
  "heartbeat": "Field BAS Comm. Status (BV 110) must change state before the BAS Comm. Lost Delay (AV 103, default 60 s) runs out, or BAS Communication Lost (BV 107) and the BAS LOST alarm (BV 899) are set. Enable BAS Monitor Schedule (BV 106) lets the unit fall back to its local schedule on a loss. The manual does not describe the OAT/OARH loss action beyond its status point (BV 1102).",
  "remote_sensors": "The BAS can write zone temperature (ZAT From BAS, AV 208), zone RH (AV 211), CO2 (AV 213), outdoor temperature (AV 1104) and outdoor RH (AV 1106). BAS outdoor values are monitored when Enable BAS Mon OAT/OARH (BV 1100) is on; Local OAT/OARH Sensor Enabled (BV 1115) selects the unit's own sensors.",
  "setup": [
   "BACnet device instance defaults to 1602; with Auto Generate Device ID = Yes, the rotary switch address is added to 1602. Set it on the Equipment Touch (BAS Set Up > Communication).",
   "MS/TP on Port S1 (Port S1 rotary switch = 1) or Port S2; MAC 0-127 on the three rotary switches; baud default 76.8k or autobaud.",
   "BACnet IP or BACnet Ethernet on the Gig-E port; IP by DHCP, custom static, or default 192.168.168.x from the rotary switches.",
   "Set the port's End of Net? switch to Yes at either end of an MS/TP segment.",
   "Service port web pages at http://169.254.1.1 (laptop 169.254.1.2-7, mask 255.255.255.248)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "BAS Manual Occ Control only works when Occupancy Control is set to BAS control.",
   "The PID Output Override and Override Lock points (SF, EF, OADA, heat, HGRH) fix outputs for CAV setups; don't write them for normal control.",
   "Operating mode and condition are integer AVs; see the Appendix B code lists in the notes.",
   "To use the unit with Carrier i-Vu Open it needs an i-Vu Link and i-Vu Open Plus."
  ]
 },
